decompose(BettiTally) -- write a Betti diagram as a positive combination of pure integral diagrams
**************************************************************************************************

  * Function: *note decompose: (Macaulay2Doc)decompose,
  * Usage: 
        decompose B
  * Inputs:
      * B, a *note Betti tally: (Macaulay2Doc)BettiTally,, not necessarily
        Cohen-Macaulay
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * TableEntries (missing documentation) => ..., default value
        LeastIntegerEntries,
  * Outputs:
      * an *note expression: (Macaulay2Doc)Expression,, a positive combination
        of pure integral Betti diagrams

Description
===========

This applies the algorithm implied by the Boij-Soederberg conjecture, and also
works even if the diagram does not corresponds to a Cohen-Macaulay module.
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = ZZ/103[a,b,c]                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o1 = R                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : I = ideal"a3,abc,b4,c4,b2c2"                                            |
|                                                                             |
|             3          4   4   2 2                                          |
|o2 = ideal (a , a*b*c, b , c , b c )                                         |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : Ideal of R                                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : B = betti res I                                                         |
|                                                                             |
|            0 1 2 3                                                          |
|o3 = total: 1 5 8 4                                                          |
|         0: 1 . . .                                                          |
|         1: . . . .                                                          |
|         2: . 2 . .                                                          |
|         3: . 3 2 .                                                          |
