matrix(BettiTally,ZZ,ZZ) -- Betti diagram to matrix
***************************************************

  * Function: *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)matrix,
  * Usage: 
        matrix B
        matrix(B,lowDegree)
        matrix(B,lowDegree,highDegree)
  * Inputs:
      * B, a *note Betti tally: (Macaulay2Doc)BettiTally,
      * lowDegree, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,
      * highDegree, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note Degree: (Macaulay2Doc)matrix_lpList_rp, => ..., default value
        null,
  * Outputs:
      * a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, The Betti diagram as a matrix

Description
===========

If either lowDegree or highDegree is not given, then they are inferred from the
Betti diagram itself.  The result matrix has highDegree-lowDegree+1 rows,
corresponding to these (slanted) degrees.
+-----------------------------------+
|i1 : B = pureBettiDiagram {0,1,4,7}|
|                                   |
|            0  1 2 3               |
|o1 = total: 9 14 7 2               |
|         0: 9 14 . .               |
|         1: .  . . .               |
|         2: .  . 7 .               |
|         3: .  . . .               |
|         4: .  . . 2               |
|                                   |
|o1 : BettiTally                    |
+-----------------------------------+
|i2 : matrix B                      |
|                                   |
|o2 = | 9 14 0 0 |                  |
|     | 0 0  0 0 |                  |
|     | 0 0  7 0 |                  |
|     | 0 0  0 0 |                  |
|     | 0 0  0 2 |                  |
|                                   |
|              5       4            |
|o2 : Matrix ZZ  <-- ZZ             |
+-----------------------------------+
|i3 : matrix(B,-2)                  |
|                                   |
|o3 = | 0 0  0 0 |                  |
|     | 0 0  0 0 |                  |
|     | 9 14 0 0 |                  |
|     | 0 0  0 0 |                  |
|     | 0 0  7 0 |                  |
|     | 0 0  0 0 |                  |
|     | 0 0  0 2 |                  |
|                                   |
|              7       4            |
|o3 : Matrix ZZ  <-- ZZ             |
+-----------------------------------+
|i4 : matrix(B,-2,5)                |
|                                   |
|o4 = | 0 0  0 0 |                  |
|     | 0 0  0 0 |                  |
|     | 9 14 0 0 |                  |
|     | 0 0  0 0 |                  |
|     | 0 0  7 0 |                  |
|     | 0 0  0 0 |                  |
|     | 0 0  0 2 |                  |
|     | 0 0  0 0 |                  |
|                                   |
|              8       4            |
|o4 : Matrix ZZ  <-- ZZ             |
+-----------------------------------+
This function is essentially the inverse of *note mat2betti:
mat2betti_lpMatrix_cmZZ_rp,.
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i5 : R = ZZ/101[a..e];                         |
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i6 : I = ideal borel monomialIdeal"abc,ad3,e4";|
|                                               |
|o6 : Ideal of R                                |
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i7 : B = betti res I                           |
|                                               |
