pureWeyman -- first Betti number of specific exact complex
**********************************************************

  * Usage: 
        pureWeyman L
  * Inputs:
      * a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, a strictly increasing sequence of
        degrees
  * Outputs:
      * an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, The zero-th Betti number of the
        corresponding pure resolution construction

Description
===========

*note pureWeyman: pureWeyman, corresponds to the construction in
math.AC/0709.1529v3 "The Existence of Pure Free Resolutions", Section 4.
+-----------------------------+
|i1 : L = {0,2,3,9}           |
|                             |
|o1 = {0, 2, 3, 9}            |
|                             |
|o1 : List                    |
+-----------------------------+
|i2 : B = pureBettiDiagram L  |
|                             |
|            0  1  2 3        |
|o2 = total: 7 27 21 1        |
|         0: 7  .  . .        |
|         1: . 27 21 .        |
|         2: .  .  . .        |
|         3: .  .  . .        |
|         4: .  .  . .        |
|         5: .  .  . .        |
|         6: .  .  . 1        |
|                             |
|o2 : BettiTally              |
+-----------------------------+
|i3 : pureWeyman L            |
|                             |
|o3 = 21                      |
+-----------------------------+
|i4 : L1 = {0,3,5,6}          |
|                             |
|o4 = {0, 3, 5, 6}            |
|                             |
|o4 : List                    |
+-----------------------------+
|i5 : B1 = pureBettiDiagram L1|
|                             |
|            0 1 2 3          |
|o5 = total: 1 5 9 5          |
|         0: 1 . . .          |
|         1: . . . .          |
|         2: . 5 . .          |
|         3: . . 9 5          |
|                             |
|o5 : BettiTally              |
+-----------------------------+
|i6 : pureWeyman L1           |
|                             |
|o6 = 3                       |
+-----------------------------+
Thus, for large enough multiples m, m*B occurs as the Betti diagram of a module
in the Weyman construction


